// Title: Remote Access Tool - Cmd.EXE Execution via AnyViewer
// Sigma ID: bc533330-fc29-44c0-b245-7dc6e5939c87
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: @kostastsale
// Date: 2024-08-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, persistence
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects execution of "cmd.exe" via the AnyViewer RMM agent on a remote management sessions.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use for admin activity.
// References:
//   - https://www.anyviewer.com/help/remote-technical-support.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_remote_access_tools_anyviewer_shell_exec.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\AVCore.exe" and InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "AVCore.exe\" -d" and FolderPath endswith "\\cmd.exe"
